course: dictionary
lesson: 5867
title: The Manchu and the Qing dynasty
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Manchu is the name of a people. The Manchu come from Manchuria, in north-east China. The capital M shows it is a name, like Scottish or Chinese.
explain: Manchu can also be the name of their language. As an adjective, Manchu describes things that belong to the Manchu people, such as their customs.
explain: Read the context: «The Qing dynasty, 1644–1912, was founded by the Manchus from the northeast.» Founded means started, so the Manchus started the Qing dynasty. A dynasty is a line of rulers from the same family, so the Manchu ruled China as the Qing dynasty from 1644 to 1912.
fact: Manchu means a people from Manchuria in north-east China.
fact: Manchu is also the name of their language.
fact: The Manchu ruled China as the Qing dynasty from 1644 to 1912.
fact: «The Manchus ruled through Chinese institutions and kept Manchu customs.» Both things were true at the same time.
fact: Manchu is written with a capital M because it is the name of a people.
exercise: «The Qing dynasty ... was founded by the Manchus from the northeast.» What does founded mean? | Destroyed | Painted | Forgotten | *Started
exercise: Where did the Manchu come from? | A small island in the Pacific | *Manchuria, in north-east China | Southern England | The middle of the Sahara
exercise: «...made men wear the queue, a shaved forehead with a long braid.» What was the queue? | A type of boat | *A shaved forehead with a long braid | A tall hat with feathers | A red silk coat
test: The Manchu ruled China as the Qing dynasty. From which years? | From 1914 to 1918 | *From 1644 to 1912 | Between 1066 and 1485 | From 1800 to 1850
test: Manchu is also the name of their | river | *language | castle | mountain
exam: The Manchu came from Manchuria. Which country is Manchuria in? | Japan | *China | Russia | England
